WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.638
A landing zone, as Cloud Boundary
and Landing Zone designs it,

3
00:00:04.638 --> 00:00:08.144
decides what can be deployed:
the management group hierarchy,

4
00:00:08.144 --> 00:00:12.475
the boundary policies, and the provisioning
loop every change goes through.

5
00:00:12.475 --> 00:00:15.521
What it doesn't decide is
what the internet can reach,

6
00:00:15.521 --> 00:00:18.000
what leaves the estate,
or who can read a key.

7
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.513
Those are engineered one service at a
time, and each one has to be proved.

8
00:00:22.513 --> 00:00:24.312
The proving starts with a list.

9
00:00:24.312 --> 00:00:28.487
You can't show that every public
endpoint sits behind DDoS protection

10
00:00:28.487 --> 00:00:32.662
and a web application firewall if
you don't know every public endpoint.

11
00:00:32.662 --> 00:00:36.668
So this module adds the security
settings the baseline needs,

12
00:00:36.668 --> 00:00:41.040
and builds the exposure register
that Modules 2 to 5 check against.
